{
  "bridge_text": "寒冷的冬夜里，莉娜站在那棵比教堂还要高大的空心树下，感受着树皮里传出的阵阵低吟，她决定去探寻大人们闭口不谈的秘密。",
  "resume_strategy": "restart",
  "replacement_segments": [
    {
      "id": "s1",
      "text": "在莉娜居住的小村庄边缘，矗立着一棵比教堂还高的空心树。每到冬天的夜晚，树皮里就会传出低沉的嗡嗡声，大人们总是告诫孩子们离它远点。但在奶奶没讲完故事就睡着的那个晚上，莉娜穿上红色羊毛大衣，穿过结霜的田野，独自走向那棵神秘的树去一探究竟。"
    },
    {
      "id": "s2",
      "text": "在空心树的内部，她发现了一圈盘旋向下的楼梯，最上面的台阶上坐着一只穿着补丁绿背心的老灰狐狸，它叫莫斯克。他用落叶般沙哑的声音告诉莉娜，这棵树不是用来参观的，她应该回家忘掉那些声音。可莉娜却坚定地说，她无法忘掉那些还没听真切的旋律。"
    },
    {
      "id": "s3",
      "text": "莫斯克指着门口示意她离开，莉娜却从口袋里掏出了这季最后一颗苹果，轻轻放在他们之间的台阶上。她说这是为了麻烦他带她走下楼梯的谢礼。莫斯克盯着那颗苹果看了很久，最后他站起身，系好背心，一言不发地踏上了第一级台阶。"
    }
  ],
  "active_scene_id": "s1"
}

{
  "bridge_text": "Even if Mosk the fox seems a bit grumpy right now, his secrets are tucked deep within his patched green vest. Let us see if he can truly turn Lina away from the humming.",
  "resume_strategy": "continue",
  "replacement_segments": [
    {
      "id": "s2",
      "text": "Mosk told her, in a voice like dry leaves, that the tree was not for visiting and that she should go home and forget the humming. Lina stood her ground, telling the old fox she could not forget what she had not yet heard."
    }
  ],
  "active_scene_id": "s2"
}

{
  "bridge_text": "Now that we remember old Mosk and his patched green vest, we must see what he does next. He was quite serious about Lina leaving, but she was not ready to go.",
  "resume_strategy": "skip",
  "replacement_segments": [
    {
      "id": "s3",
      "text": "Mosk pointed sternly at the door, but Lina reached into her pocket and pulled out the very last apple of the season. She set the bright red fruit on the step between them and told him it was for the trouble of walking her down. Mosk stared at the apple for a long time before he finally stood up, tied his vest, and stepped onto the first stair without a word."
    },
    {
      "id": "s4",
      "text": "At the bottom of the stairs the humming became a quiet song, where a firefly the size of a robin lay on a bed of soft moss. Her glow was almost out, and Mosk's whiskers trembled at the sight. He whispered that she had been his friend once, but he had failed to bring her medicine one winter long ago and had stayed to guard the tree out of shame."
    }
  ],
  "active_scene_id": "s3"
}

{
